{
  "note": [
    "The Robot Shop's fabric (DR-106, the mech wing), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. 8 x 3.6 x 10, the eye at the middle. The game: \"This room, with exits west and northwest, is filled with robot-like devices of every conceivable description, all in various states of disassembly\" (compone.zil 1826-1828); Floyd starts here (1838-1843) -- an overlay, not painted.",
    "Benches along the east wall with torsos and a head on them, a half-built robot standing in the north-east, one on its back to the south, racks of limbs on the south wall, a heap of parts in the south-west corner, a charging cabinet on the north wall; the floor west of the eye open. Both doorways, 1.6 x 2.4, are in the west wall (cut once, the pier put back): north-west, 3.9 m north of the eye, onto Mech Corridor South; west, 0.72 m south, onto the Machine Shop and, in line through it, the Tool Room's shelving 16 m off."
  ],
